Harness profile and probe reflector (`src/harness/`, `src/workflows/prompts/probe-reflect.ts`)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Source: google-research/harness2, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (https://github.com/google-research/harness2). Files consulted: `harness2/core/prompts.py` (the `experience` prompt, about lines 1105-1164; SHA-256 of the consulted file `d1f4f8db4ab4cb4addcbca175b548db2270375499fda727ac95d271c63cc2504`) and the eight-component harness taxonomy in `harness2/substrate/opencode.py` (c1 system prompt, c2 guardrails, c3 memory, c4 tool guidance, c5 sub-agents, c6 skills, c7 scripts, c8 plugins/hooks).
- `probe-reflect.ts` adapts ideas and some phrasing of that prompt: treat every candidate as evidence rather than only the adopted one, prefer `confounded` over an invented attribution, a cue that names the shape of a situation, a lesson that names the component it concerns, and an explicit NO_ENTRY. It was changed substantially: verdicts are computed by code from recorded deterministic verify outcomes and the model may only cite rows code marked helped or hurt; the reply is one JSON object that code re-validates; nothing is edited by the reflector.
- `harness/profile.ts` reuses only the c1..c8 vocabulary. In Otter c1, c2, c4, c5, c7 and c8 are code-owned and not proposable, and the only proposable surface is task-data approach overlay text (INV/DOM), which never enters role policy identity.
- No harness2 code is copied, and no result from the harness2 paper is claimed or reproduced here. Modified portions of the adapted prompt text are marked by this notice; the full Apache-2.0 text is at https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.

