- Otter deliberately differs: harness2 lets a model edit eight harness components (system prompt, guardrails, memory, tool guidance, sub-agents, skills, scripts, plugins/hooks). Here a model proposes ONLY a short approach-overlay text (at most 1200 bytes) carried as task data in the worker's user message; system prompts, guardrails, tool guidance, roles, scripts, plugins, hooks and skills are never proposable and role policy ids are identical across base/inv/dom. Proposals come from read-only roles, nothing runs until a typed approval matches the exact subject sha256, every probe runs once in its own isolated worktree and is never merged automatically, commands run only through the framework verifier, outcomes are classified by code, and a human chooses (Apply, Keep or Discard). There is no model selector or judge, no automatic adoption and no composed overlay. No harness2 code is copied and no harness2 paper result is claimed.

